## Background: The Paradigm Shift

### Privacy-Preserving vs Privacy-Enabling

**Privacy-Preserving (Current Dominant Paradigm)**

- Organizations protect data they control
- Top-down, controller-centric approach
- Focus: Companies implementing better safeguards (encryption, anonymization, differential privacy)
- Problem: Individuals remain dependent on organizational protection decisions

**Privacy-Enabling (Emerging Paradigm)**

- Individuals control whether to share data
- Bottom-up, individual-centric approach
- Focus: Controller-ID first architecture enabling "architecture I choose to trust"
- Solution: Transparency infrastructure enables individual data control

### Why This Matters

Current privacy frameworks cannot measure or enforce transparency at scale. This workshop presents evidence-based regulatory capacity innovation.

