## Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Is this about making Chrome compliant?**

No. This workshop demonstrates systemic governance failure requiring regulatory capacity innovation, not vendor-specific fixes.

**Q: Who developed TPI-R methodology?**

TPI-R methodology derives from ISO/IEC 27560 consent record information structure and Convention 108+ transparency requirements.

**Q: What happens after the workshop?**

Q2 2026 CoE consultation and Q3 2026 UN/CEFACT liaison will advance international coordination. GitHub repository provides technical implementation resources.

**Q: Is UNRP available now?**

ISO/IEC 27560-1 Universal Notice Receipt Profile is under development. March 2026 plenary will advance the standard.

**Q: Can I implement Controller-ID first architecture today?**

Yes. Level 1 (Self-Assertion) uses open MVCR to add notice.txt, notice event log, and CIR. No registration required.

**Q: How does this relate to GDPR/PIPEDA/other regulations?**

UNRP provides transparency infrastructure compatible with all major privacy frameworks. Convention 108+ integration ensures broad jurisdictional coverage.

